{#
  One dialog shared by every "who…?" list on the page — the reaction
  tallies and the "vu par" lines alike. Its trigger fetches the rendered
  list, sets the title from its own `data-dialog-title`, and fills the
  body with the response (public/assets/js/groups.js), rather than every
  post and reply carrying a dialog of its own.

  The title starts on the commonest of the two so a dialog opened before
  the title is set still says something true.
#}
<div class="modal fade" id="groups-detail-modal" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="groups-detail-modal-label" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered">
        <div class="modal-content">
            <div class="modal-header">
                <h2 class="modal-title h5" id="groups-detail-modal-label">Réactions</h2>
                <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Fermer"></button>
            </div>
            <div class="modal-body" id="groups-detail-modal-body">
                <div class="text-center py-3">
                    <span class="spinner-border spinner-border-sm" role="status" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
